  {
    "clock": {
      "at": "1885-02-10T09:00",
      "note": "'this life lasted ten years': all of this is one summarised stretch"
    },
    "edit": {
      "turn": 9,
      "events": [
        {
          "turn": 9,
          "round": 1,
          "text": "Mme. Loisel took her part with heroism: they dismissed their servant, changed their lodgings and rented a garret; she did the heavy house-work, washed dishes and linen, carried water and slops, and bargained with the shopkeepers sou by sou, while each month they met notes and Loisel copied accounts in the evening and manuscripts at night for five sous a page.",
          "importance": 5,
          "tags": [
            "poverty",
            "labour",
            "housework",
            "ten-years"
          ],
          "involves": [
            "mathilde",
            "loisel",
            "servant",
            "lenders"
          ],
          "perceived_by": [
            {
              "character": "mathilde",
              "mode": "witnessed"
            },
            {
              "character": "loisel",
              "mode": "witnessed"
            }
          ],
          "location": "garret"
        },
        {
          "turn": 9,
          "round": 2,
          "text": "At the end of ten years they had paid everything, with usurers' rates and compound interest.",
          "importance": 5,
          "tags": [
            "debt",
            "paid",
            "ten-years"
          ],
          "involves": [
            "mathilde",
            "loisel",
            "lenders"
          ],
          "perceived_by": [
            {
              "character": "mathilde",
              "mode": "witnessed"
            },
            {
              "character": "loisel",
              "mode": "witnessed"
            }
          ],
          "location": "garret"
        },
        {
          "turn": 9,
          "round": 3,
          "text": "Mme. Loisel looked old now, strong and hard and rough; sometimes, when her husband was at the office, she sat by the window and thought of that evening, and of what might have happened if she had not lost the necklace.",
          "importance": 4,
          "tags": [
